<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="010" project="spaarkeai-compose-r7">
  <metadata>
    <title>Introduce a stable, non-rotating logical document id persisted across re-mounts (FR-07b)</title>
    <phase>1 Save-Identity Fix (UC-8)</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .tsx/.ts client code and a contract type; architectural foundation that blocks Phase 4 (draft key) and the client dedup key.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Architectural change — introduces a new cross-cutting identity concept persisted through 4 mount/persist-back paths; blocks Phase 4 and the FR-07 dedup key. Blast radius across ComposeWorkspace lifecycle.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches ComposeWorkspace.tsx / ComposeWorkspace.types.ts + compose-contracts.ts (shared Compose spine + cross-worktree contention per INDEX.md).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>frontend, react, typescript, refactoring</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Introduce a stable, non-rotating logical document id that survives widget re-mount and reload for an unsaved Compose
    document. Today no such id exists: transientKey is minted fresh at every transient/draft mount door and never persisted,
    speDriveItemId is reset to '' on transient mounts, and sprkDocumentId exists only after first-save promotion. Persist and
    rehydrate a single logical id so the same document keeps one identity across re-mount/reload. This id is the SHARED key
    for both the FR-03 draft-recovery store and the FR-07 client dedup path.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in React lifecycle, the Compose workspace mount/persist-back state machine, and TypeScript contract types. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>
    ComposeDocumentRef carries a non-rotating logical id (either a persisted transientKey or a new composeLogicalId field) that:
    is minted once per logical document, persisted to local/session storage, and rehydrated on re-mount/reload; is written back
    through saveSucceeded / mountTransient / mountDraftHtml / loadSucceeded; and is exposed as the derivation
    `sprkDocumentId ?? speDriveItemId ?? persistedLogicalId` for downstream consumers (FR-03 draft store, FR-07 dedup).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec.md FR-07(b) + §11 New-Components table. Owner clarification: unify FR-03 draft-recovery + FR-07 client dedup on ONE
      stable id. Confirmed against code: none of speDriveItemId / sprkDocumentId / transientKey is non-rotating pre-save.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.types.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">ComposeWorkspace.tsx mint sites @2962/3011/3289/3347/3420/1113 via mintTransientKey@240 — the fresh-mint doors to unify onto one persisted id</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">ComposeWorkspace.types.ts mountTransient@559, mountDraftHtml@613 (speDriveItemId reset), saveSucceeded / loadSucceeded persist-back</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">compose-contracts.ts ComposeDocumentRef@642–668 (speDriveItemId / sprkDocumentId@646 / transientKey)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Coordination gate + conflict-check clean on the Compose spine.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">The logical id is a CLIENT identity concept only; it MUST NOT change the server save/version contract (ADR-049 append-only SPE versioning is unchanged by this task).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The persisted id MUST be non-rotating for a given logical document across ALL transient/draft mount doors — do not mint a fresh key on re-mount when a persisted one exists.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Expose the exact derivation `sprkDocumentId ?? speDriveItemId ?? persistedLogicalId` as the single identity accessor consumed by FR-03 (040) and FR-07 client dedup (011). Do NOT create two divergent keys.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT delete docxBridge.ts. MUST NOT add a server-side draft/identity store — this id lives client-side (local/session storage).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Prefer extending ComposeDocumentRef / the existing transientKey plumbing over adding a parallel identity mechanism (root §11).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>compose mount identity, client persistence</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/COMPOSE-READ-REFERENCE-FIDELITY.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL, model-tier opus; load ADR-049 + spec.md FR-07.</step>
    <step order="1">Trace the six mint sites (@2962/3011/3289/3347/3420/1113) and the mintTransientKey@240 helper; confirm none persists.</step>
    <step order="2">Decide the implementation: persist the transientKey vs add a dedicated composeLogicalId field on ComposeDocumentRef. Document the bounded choice in notes/.</step>
    <step order="3">Add persistence (local/session storage) + rehydration keyed so a re-mount/reload for the same logical document resolves the SAME id.</step>
    <step order="4">Wire the persist-back through saveSucceeded / mountTransient / mountDraftHtml / loadSucceeded so the id survives each transition.</step>
    <step order="5">Expose the `sprkDocumentId ?? speDriveItemId ?? persistedLogicalId` derivation as the identity accessor for FR-03/FR-07.</step>
    <step order="6">Add/adjust unit tests for id stability across a simulated re-mount and across each persist-back transition.</step>
    <step order="7">Run jest for the Compose widget suite; verify green.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set 010 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Record the implementation choice + any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If persisting transientKey turns out to require touching the server save/promote contract (i.e., the id cannot stay client-only), STOP and escalate (root §6.5 — this would breach the client-only decision and NFR-03) rather than adding a server field.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>ComposeDocumentRef (compose-contracts.ts:642–668) has speDriveItemId / sprkDocumentId@646 / transientKey — but none is non-rotating pre-save (confirmed in spec §11).</existing>
    <extension>Extend the existing ComposeDocumentRef + transientKey plumbing (persist it) rather than a parallel identity object; a dedicated composeLogicalId field is acceptable only if persisting transientKey proves infeasible — it is still an extension of the same ref, not a new subsystem.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without a non-rotating id, FR-03 draft recovery orphans drafts on re-mount and FR-07 client dedup has no stable key — duplicate sprk_document rows recur and unsaved drafts are lost. This blocks Phase 4 entirely.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Draft identity survives re-mount">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a new (unsaved) Compose document; note its logical id via the identity accessor.</step>
        <step>Unmount and re-mount the Compose widget (simulate tab switch / reload).</step>
        <step>Verify the identity accessor returns the SAME id, and no fresh transientKey was minted.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The logical id is identical before and after re-mount; storage holds one entry per logical document.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build/test the Spaarke.Compose.Components package (build:prod semantics for shared lib)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.types.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts</output>
    <output type="test">Compose widget unit tests for id stability</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a new unsaved doc, when the widget re-mounts or the page reloads, then the identity accessor returns the same logical id (no fresh mint).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The id is written back through saveSucceeded, mountTransient, mountDraftHtml, and loadSucceeded (each transition preserves it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The identity accessor implements exactly `sprkDocumentId ?? speDriveItemId ?? persistedLogicalId`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The id lives entirely client-side (local/session storage); no server contract or BFF endpoint was changed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">docxBridge.ts is not deleted; no parallel identity mechanism was added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Compose widget jest suite passes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-07(b), §11 table row "Stable logical document id", Owner Clarifications "Draft-identity key". Implementation choice (persist transientKey vs new composeLogicalId) is a bounded design detail left to this task.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
